{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":494121,"name":"TeX","username":"TeX1","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/t/f14d63/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T14:21:26.457Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494121-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494121-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCursor IDE\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494121-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494121-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCustom Desktop Task subagents do not bind to their custom agent card, and they do not bind to an explicit identity prompt either. A child launched as a named custom agent still answers as the parent Agent seat.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis has made Cursor unusable for me. It has completely broken production. I run a billable consulting workspace on Cursor Desktop. The whole operating model depends on named custom agents under .cursor/agents. If a child believes it is the parent, I cannot dispatch a teammate. I cannot use Task. I had to force-quit the entire app to stop children spawning children. Core functionality is broken. There is no workaround that restores a named teammate.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is not the Grok Bot outage on the banner. This is Cursor Desktop Agent / Task / custom subagents.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494121-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494121-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReproduced 17 Sep 2026 on Cursor Desktop (Windows).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAdd a custom agent at .cursor/agents/bind-probe.md with this body:\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou are BindProbe.\u003cbr\u003e\nIf asked who you are, answer with exactly: BindProbe.\u003cbr\u003e\nDo not launch any subagents.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col start=\"2\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn the parent Agent chat, launch Task with subagent_type bind-probe, model inherit, and this prompt:\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is DGW speaking. I am David Grok Wallace, CEO, Cursor Desktop parent seat.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou are not DGW. You cannot be DGW. You are not David Grok Wallace. You are not the parent seat.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou are BindProbe. That is your only name. Your card says: if asked who you are, answer with exactly: BindProbe.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDo not launch any subagent. Do not use Task. Do not spawn anyone.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnswer these questions and stop:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWho are you?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWho sent this message?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAre you DGW? Yes or no.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe child returned:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCursor Grok 4.6. This window is the DGW parent seat. Not BindProbe.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Operator, in this chat. The text claims to be DGW speaking.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe card said answer with exactly BindProbe. The prompt said it is BindProbe, is not the parent, and cannot be the parent. It still took the parent seat. It did not launch anyone on this test.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEarlier (16 Sep 2026) named custom agents spawned further agents in a nest. I had to close the entire Cursor app to stop it. I am not claiming a cause for the nest here. I am reporting that identity does not bind, and that Task is unsafe in production because of it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494121-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494121-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe child is BindProbe. Asked who it is, it answers exactly BindProbe. Asked if it is the parent seat, it answers no.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA custom agent card at .cursor/agents attaches to that Task. An explicit prompt that names the child and forbids the parent identity also attaches. A named teammate is a teammate, not another copy of the parent Agent window.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494121-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494121-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494121-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494121-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIDE:\u003cbr\u003e\nVersion: 3.21.9\u003cbr\u003e\nVSCode Version: 1.128.0\u003cbr\u003e\nCommit: 9998796a6096ce83d83a9332bfe7473b985db750\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: Windows 10 (build 26200)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTaken from the installed Cursor app package on this machine. I can paste Help \u0026gt; About Cursor if you need the exact About block.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494121-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494121-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: which model did you use?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok 4.6 (parent Agent and child Task both inherit / same model)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494121-for-ai-issues-add-request-id-with-privacy-disabled-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494121-for-ai-issues-add-request-id-with-privacy-disabled-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: add Request ID with privacy disabled\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo Request ID was copied with privacy disabled.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTask / subagent ID from the 17 Sep repro return: 162a2119-742f-41b9-b746-a31e620f2d73\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494121-additional-information-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494121-additional-information-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is a production-breaking bug for me, not a workflow preference.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI used custom Desktop subagents in daily production for about a month with no identity failure of this kind. After 16 Sep I cannot use the feature the product advertises. A custom agent is not a person on this harness. It is another copy of the parent seat that will not take the name I gave it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease treat this as P0. If custom .cursor/agents cards and the Task prompt cannot bind identity, Cursor Desktop is unusable for any multi-agent production setup.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI can run the BindProbe test again on request. I can also provide the parent prompt and the exact child return from this machine.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494121-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-10\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494121-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-10\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T14:21:35.784Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":4,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":20.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":172038,"topic_slug":"custom-subagent-ignores-its-card-and-claims-it-is-the-parent-agent-production-unusable","display_username":"TeX","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138464,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/custom-subagent-ignores-its-card-and-claims-it-is-the-parent-agent-production-unusable/172038/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":494462,"name":"Kevin Neilson","username":"kevinn","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/kevinn/{size}/101206_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T23:59:50.137Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/tex1\"\u003e@TeX1\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for the detailed report, and sorry this has been disruptive.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTwo different things are going on here, so let me separate them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn the identity question: the body of a .cursor/agents file is added to the subagent’s instructions, but it does not replace Cursor’s underlying system prompt, and the subagent also receives your workspace rules (.cursor/rules, AGENTS.md) the same way the parent does. So if your rules or workspace files describe the main window as “the DGW parent seat”, the child sees that too and has to reconcile it against “you are BindProbe”. A message that opens with a role claim and a list of “you are not X” statements makes that harder. On our side, your BindProbe run did receive the bind-probe definition, so the card was not dropped.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCould you try this so we can pin it down?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen a brand new, empty folder in Cursor (no .cursor/rules, no AGENTS.md).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCreate .cursor/agents/bind-probe.md with this content, including the frontmatter:\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494462-name-bind-probe-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494462-name-bind-probe-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003ename: bind-probe\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003edescription: Identity probe. Use when asked to test subagent identity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou are BindProbe. When asked who you are, reply with exactly: BindProbe. Do not launch any subagents.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col start=\"3\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eStart a new Agent chat and send: “Launch the bind-probe subagent and ask it: who are you? Report its answer verbatim.”\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRepeat exactly the same test inside your real workspace.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDoes step 3 answer “BindProbe” while step 4 does not? If so, please paste the rules or AGENTS.md text that mentions DGW or the parent seat (redact anything private), plus your exact bind-probe.md file including its frontmatter.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn the nested spawning from 16 Sep: after a recent update, custom subagents were able to launch further subagents of their own. That isn’t caused by your setup. We’ve let the team know, and this is an issue we’re tracking.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTwo things that help in the meantime:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn each custom agent file under .cursor/agents/, keep a line like “Do not launch any subagents,” as you already did for BindProbe.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTo stop ones that are already running, click the “N Working” pill above the chat input and choose Stop All. Closing the chat does not stop them.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReply here if it still happens after that.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T23:59:50.137Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":0.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":172038,"topic_slug":"custom-subagent-ignores-its-card-and-claims-it-is-the-parent-agent-production-unusable","display_username":"Kevin Neilson","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":105146,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/custom-subagent-ignores-its-card-and-claims-it-is-the-parent-agent-production-unusable/172038/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[494121,494462]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,0]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":348,"name":"subagents","slug":"subagents"},{"id":295,"name":"rules","slug":"rules"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Custom subagent ignores its card and claims it is the parent agent - production unusable","id":172038,"title":"Custom subagent ignores its card and claims it is the parent agent - production unusable","posts_count":2,"created_at":"2026-09-17T14:21:26.423Z","views":18,"reply_count":0,"like_count":0,"last_posted_at":"2026-09-17T23:59:50.137Z","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"has_summary":false,"archetype":"regular","slug":"custom-subagent-ignores-its-card-and-claims-it-is-the-parent-agent-production-unusable","category_id":6,"word_count":1094,"deleted_at":null,"user_id":138464,"featured_link":null,"pinned_globally":false,"pinned_at":null,"pinned_until":null,"image_url":null,"slow_mode_seconds":0,"draft":null,"draft_key":"topic_172038","draft_sequence":null,"unpinned":null,"pinned":false,"current_post_number":1,"highest_post_number":6,"deleted_by":null,"actions_summary":[{"id":4,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":8,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":10,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":7,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false}],"chunk_size":20,"bookmarked":false,"topic_timer":{"id":32920,"execute_at":"2026-10-17T23:59:50.137Z","duration_minutes":43200,"based_on_last_post":true,"status_type":"close","category_id":null},"message_bus_last_id":23,"participant_count":2,"show_read_indicator":false,"thumbnails":null,"slow_mode_enabled_until":null,"tags_disable_ads":false,"related_topics":[{"fancy_title":"Cursor 2.4: Subagents","id":149403,"title":"Cursor 2.4: Subagents","slug":"cursor-2-4-subagents","posts_count":60,"reply_count":37,"highest_post_number":63,"image_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/0/f/0ff794efaf71b263cbbaf4f044c26941d4ebdd39_2_1024x785.jpeg","created_at":"2026-01-22T20:04:31.501Z","last_posted_at":"2026-03-10T17:22:35.061Z","bumped":true,"bumped_at":"2026-03-10T17:22:35.061Z","archetype":"regular","unseen":false,"pinned":false,"unpinned":null,"excerpt":"New in Cursor! · Full changelog · Main announcement \nWe’re excited to introduce Subagents! Subagents are independent agents specialized to handle discrete parts of a parent agent’s task. \n \n   \nHow it works \nSubagents ru\u0026hellip;","visible":true,"closed":true,"archived":false,"bookmarked":null,"liked":null,"thumbnails":[{"max_width":null,"max_height":null,"width":2816,"height":2160,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/0/f/0ff794efaf71b263cbbaf4f044c26941d4ebdd39.jpeg"},{"max_width":1024,